title: AfterMemory
// Corresponds to scene 8 in the narrative script
// Ruzica = char 1
// Jovan = char 2

// NOTE: Jovan used to be char 1, and is still lover1 because he appears first in the past.
    // The character order was switch last minute for the 4/10/2026 build.
    // The past was originally planned to be first-person POV, but was changed.
    // Jovan's cousin had to be on the left in the past to sit in the chair,
    // so keeping Jovan on the right added the most visual consistency.
---
<<declare $CousinName = "Sasha">>
<<changeSprite 1 0>>
<<changeSprite 2 0>>
<<twoChar>>
{$lover1Name} and {$lover2Name} sit in silence for a while.
<<darken 2>>
<<darken 1>>

-> Ask about {$CousinName}.
    {$protagName}: So you got out, but what happened to Sasha?
    <<jump Sasha>>
-> Ask where they went.
    {$protagName}: Where did you go?
    <<jump Away>>
-> Wait for them to continue.
    <<jump Silence>>
===

title: Sasha
---
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} opens and closes his mouth as if to speak.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}:  We can never repay {$CousinName} for what he did for us.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: He died-
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: {$lover1Name}...
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: They burned his house and he died.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} glares at you.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} closes his eyes.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: {$CousinName} is why we're here. He deserved to be remembered.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}'s expression softens.
{$lover2Name}: We stopped by a bakery to buy his favorite cake.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} smiles.
{$lover1Name}: He loved chocolate cake. It drove our family crazy. He never shared either.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} smiles too.
{$lover2Name}: Sasha had a good taste in dessert.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} turns to {$lover2Name}.
{$lover1Name}: And you never told me you liked chocolate cake too!
He turns back to you.
{$lover1Name}: My own wife hid this from me for years!
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} grins.
{$lover2Name}: You're being dramatic.
She turns serious.
<<darken 1>>
<<jump Leave>>
===

title: Away
---
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: We kept running until we got to another city. We ran here.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: There was a very kind woman who let us stay in her spare room for a few days. 
{$lover1Name}: Then we wrote letters to our families to let them know we were okay. 
{$lover1Name}: That's how {$CousinName}-
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: {$lover1Name}...
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: He's why we're here! 
{$lover1Name}: He took such a big risk helping us and they burned down his house.
{$lover1Name}: He died, he died for us!
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: {$CousinName} was kind. 
{$lover2Name}: I never met him, but he gave his life for us.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: He deserves to be remembered. 
{$lover1Name}: That's why we wanted to talk to you. 
{$lover1Name}: Even after we're gone, the tree will be here and so will Sasha's memory.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: But we also need to move on, even if it's hard.
{$lover2Name} focuses on {$lover1Name}.
{$lover2Name}: Remember how he was when he was alive.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} smiles.
{$lover1Name}: He loved chocolate cake. I think he would've had it for every meal if he could.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: {$CousinName} had good taste.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} focuses on {$lover2Name}.
{$lover1Name}: And you never told me you liked chocolate until <i>after</i> we left the bakery.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} smiles.
{$lover2Name}: Can't I have my secrets?
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Not about cake.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: Speaking of which,
<<darken 1>>

<<jump Leave>>
===

title: Silence
---
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Well, we don't have much else to say.
{$lover1Name}: Just please make sure you include Sasha. 
{$lover1Name}: He was important.
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: We actually stopped by the bakery to get something for him.
<<darken 1>>

<<jump Leave>>
===

title: Leave
---
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: We have to get going, the cake is going to melt.
<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: I completely forgot!
<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} smiles at {$lover1Name}.
{$lover2Name}: Of course you did.
{$lover2Name} turns back to you.
{$lover2Name}: Thank you for interviewing us. I hope our memory will look good on the tree.
<<darken 1>>
{$protagName}: I'm sure it will.
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Thank you, again. Have a good day, {$protagName}.
<<darken 2>>
-> {$protagName}: You too!
    <<jump End>>
-> {$protagName}: Thanks, I will.
    <<jump End>>
===

title: End
---
{$lover1Name} and {$lover2Name} turn and leave.
<<zeroChar>>
{$protagName}: Time to put this all together. Then I can go home.
===